# UI change verification

When editing dashboard HTML/CSS/HTMX, dashboard HTTP/static routes, or `:frontend-js` charts/DOM:

## Before calling done (and before opening a PR)

Complete these **before** `gh pr create` — never defer to “after merge”. See
`.agents/OPERATING.md` § Complete PR verifications before opening / `open-pr`.

1. **Viewport** — Judge layout at **laptop ~1280–1440px**, not only mobile. Cropped screenshots are not “mobile” unless the user says so.
2. **Cache** — Stylesheet must stay cache-busted (`/static/style.css?v=…`). New controls that look like native white buttons usually mean stale CSS.
3. **Interactions** — Prefer running `.agents/skills/ui-manual-qa` (or its STYLE/REGRESSION/HIST-ZOOM cases) after meaningful UI work; don’t rely on unit tests alone for click/zoom/view presets/scrubber pan.
4. **Visuals** — If appearance changed for README/User Guide, run docs-screenshot-refresh when shipping docs. If canonical shots are unaffected, still verify with a temp capture when claiming a visual fix.
5. **Safety chrome** — Keep the settings-backed mode plate visible on every page (`SIMULATION` > `DRY RUN` > `LIVE TRADING`). Keep stream health separate as `STREAM` / `STALE`.

After a deploy or LAN UI check, run `post-deploy-ui-smoke` (hard-refresh first).

## Common misses (regression smells)

- Missing/misleading mode plate, or stream health labeled as live trading
- Squished STREAM/STALE + relative age/time header cluster
- Dashboard hero/progress tiles clipped, empty, or missing the activity History link
- Safety cards with unclear ON/OFF state
- Concatenated deviation legend (“Over targetUnder target”)
- History Views/Zoom unstyled native buttons
- History chart title/legend/zoom header wrapping or caption/table semantics lost
- View presets that don’t hide series (Day · Total only)
- Chart drag that both zooms and pans without a separate pan control
- Scrubber stays disabled after drag/wheel zoom (only toolbar Zoom synced it)
- Scrubber thumb moves but chart does not pan (`options.scales` write ignored — need `chart.zoomScale`)
